; The four inner loops of the renderer (video.pmi), in PureMetal / PureBasic: the RP2040 (Thumb-1),
; the PC and the diagnostics include this file. The RP2350 builds include video_t2.pmi instead, the
; same four in Cortex-M33 assembly. Their inputs are the Vx Globals (an ASM block reaches a Global by
; name; a parameter lives in the procedure's stack frame), and both files must do the same thing.
; THEY RUN FROM SRAM (ProcedureRAM; the PC's CoCo3.pb makes that word an ordinary Procedure): from flash
; they shared the RP2040's XIP cache with core 0's code, and the render ran at 12 passes a second while
; core 0 waited out its frames, against 16.6 from SRAM (and core 0's emulation 10% faster), measured.

; VideoSamples (640 palette indices) to VideoOut's half at VxOutOff (480 RGB565 pixels: samples 0, 1, 2 of every four)
; through VideoPal. (Returns 0: it returned a hash of the pixels, which VideoFrame no longer uses.)
ProcedureRAM.l VideoScaleOut()
  Protected x.i
  For x = 0 To 479
    VideoOut(VxOutOff + x) = VideoPal(VideoSamples(VideoMap(x)))
  Next
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure

; Eight dots of VxGlyph (bit 7 first) at VideoSamples(VxX): VxFg where a bit is set, VxBg where it is
; clear, each VxScale (1 or 2) samples wide. VxX moves on past them.
; (The Globals are taken into locals first: on the RP2040 a loop over Globals ran the render 20% slower.)
ProcedureRAM VideoBits()
  Protected bit.i, c.i, x.i, glyph.i, fg.i, bg.i
  x = VxX : glyph = VxGlyph : fg = VxFg : bg = VxBg
  If VxScale = 2
    For bit = 7 To 0 Step -1
      If (glyph >> bit) & 1 : c = fg : Else : c = bg : EndIf
      VideoSamples(x) = c : VideoSamples(x + 1) = c : x = x + 2
    Next
  Else
    For bit = 7 To 0 Step -1
      If (glyph >> bit) & 1 : c = fg : Else : c = bg : EndIf
      VideoSamples(x) = c : x = x + 1
    Next
  EndIf
  VxX = x
EndProcedure

; VxCount bytes of graphics from the SRAM address VxSrc, VdBpp bits a pixel (high bits first), each
; pixel VxBase + its bits, VdScale samples wide, at VideoSamples(VxX). VxX moves on past them.
; With VxWords set, each byte is VideoLut's entry for it, VxWords words.
ProcedureRAM VideoGraphicsRun()
  Protected i.i, byte.i, k.i, c.i, s.i, shift.i, mask.i, ppb.i, x.i, src.i, base.i, bpp.i, scale.i, words.i, dst.i
  x = VxX : src = VxSrc : base = VxBase : bpp = VdBpp : scale = VdScale : words = VxWords
  If words
    dst = @VideoSamples(x)
    For i = 0 To VxCount - 1
      byte = PeekA(src + i) * 4
      For k = 0 To words - 1
        PokeL(dst, VideoLut(byte + k)) : dst = dst + 4
      Next
    Next
    VxX = x + VxCount * words * 4
    ProcedureReturn
  EndIf
  ppb = 8 / bpp
  mask = (1 << bpp) - 1
  For i = 0 To VxCount - 1
    byte = PeekA(src + i)
    shift = 8 - bpp
    For k = 1 To ppb
      c = base + ((byte >> shift) & mask)
      For s = 1 To scale
        VideoSamples(x) = c : x = x + 1
      Next
      shift = shift - bpp
    Next
  Next
  VxX = x
EndProcedure

; All 640 samples one palette index (the border).
ProcedureRAM VideoFill(index.i)
  Protected x.i
  For x = 0 To 639 : VideoSamples(x) = index : Next
EndProcedure

; The CRC-32 (reflected, $EDB88320) of VxCount bytes at VxSrc, carried on from VxHash, into VxHash
; (no final inversion: the result is only compared with itself).
ProcedureRAM VideoCrc()
  Protected i.i, c.l, src.i, n.i
  c = VxHash : src = VxSrc : n = VxCount
  For i = 0 To n - 1
    c = VideoCrcTab((c ! PeekA(src + i)) & 255) ! ((c >> 8) & $FFFFFF)
  Next
  VxHash = c
EndProcedure
